OL,3,AThe AI telling farmers when to harvest
OL,4,
OL,5,FWhen the first day of the apple harvest
OL,6,Frolled around in Washington State last
OL,7,Fyear, the fruit was ripe and the
OL,8,Fpickers were ready ` but the weather
OL,9,Fhad other ideas.
OL,11,F"It was like 38C... it's not safe for
OL,12,Fpeople to work in that heat," recalls
OL,13,FJoel Carter at Okanagan Specialty
OL,14,FFruits. "We had to stop at 10 o'clock
OL,15,Fin the morning."
OL,23,APub: 30-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG5/19
OL,24,ANext PageBTechnologyC Nat RadioFCulture
FL,108,105,200,160,0,100
PN,11906
SC,0006
CT,25,T
PS,c000
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F119A1790812092
OL,1,W5j 5Q#7!wsj#%uzj#57kj  7kjc1uz
OL,2,W//%*// //%Q % -,*,%%** %-.*,$-.*,%,. (,
OL,3,AThe AI telling farmers when to harvest
OL,4,
OL,5,FHe says that artificial intelligence
OL,6,F(AI) models that forecast ideal harvest
OL,7,Fdates, taking into account the weather,
OL,8,Fwould be useful. "You need to know more
OL,9,Fthan just when your fruit is going to
OL,10,Fbe ripe. How long do you have to pick
OL,11,Fit?" he says. "That's where these
OL,12,Fmodels are really helpful."
OL,14,FCarter's company has more than 1,250
OL,15,Facres of apple orchards in Washington,
OL,16,Fand the fruit is grown for sliced apple
OL,17,Fportions ` often sold to hotels and
OL,18,Fschools, for example. The firm is
OL,19,Finvesting in technology with the hope
OL,20,Fof maximising productivity. Even the
OL,21,Fapples are genetically engineered so
OL,22,Fthat they don't brown easily once cut.
OL,23,APub: 30-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG6/19
OL,24,ANext PageBTechnologyC Nat RadioFCulture
